/*
 Shadow DOM Handling:

 Where ever our Locator is present inside the Shadow DOM,
 we can directly capture the Shadow Root in SearchContext.

 If the element is a Shadow Host:

 SearchContext root = driver.findElement(locator).getShadowRoot();

 Then using that SearchContext, we can find the child element.

 If the child element is again a Shadow Host,
 again directly get the Shadow Root and store it in SearchContext.


 Example:

 SearchContext root1 =
        driver.findElement(By.cssSelector("shop-app")).getShadowRoot();

 SearchContext root2 =
        root1.findElement(By.cssSelector("shop-list")).getShadowRoot();

 SearchContext root3 =
        root2.findElement(By.cssSelector("shop-list-item")).getShadowRoot();

 WebElement price =
        root3.findElement(By.cssSelector(".price"));


 Here:

 root1 -> Shadow Root of shop-app
 root2 -> Shadow Root of shop-list
 root3 -> Shadow Root of shop-list-item

 Finally price is the WebElement present inside root3.


 Important:

 If we want to find an element inside Shadow Root,
 use SearchContext.

 If the element is again a Shadow Host,
 use getShadowRoot() again.
*/


SearchContext root1 =
        driver.findElement(By.cssSelector("shop-app")).getShadowRoot();

SearchContext root2 =
        root1.findElement(By.cssSelector("shop-list")).getShadowRoot();

SearchContext root3 =
        root2.findElement(By.cssSelector("shop-list-item")).getShadowRoot();

WebElement price =
        root3.findElement(By.cssSelector(".price"));

System.out.println(price.getText());